's not  going down very quickly and if we keep  running this out we'll find that it  stalls at a fairly high loss value so  what's going on  well when things are mostly working but  training is slow or a bit odd that can  often be a good time to look at your  optimizer and your training hyper  parameters  and this is where i want to mention one  of the most common sources of issues  when you're working with keras  you can  name things like optimizers with strings  so cara supports that and it's very  convenient but if you do that  all of the options get silently set to  their default values  so we specified our optimizer as adam  but in the process we invisibly got the  default learning rate which is 1e minus  3 or 10 to the power of -3  so this learning rate is way too high  for training transformer models we  should go back and specify the learning  rate directly not using a string so good  values here are between 1 e minus 5 and  1 e minus 4 so let's split the  difference and pick five e minus five  so if you recompile with that you'll  find that training actually works at  last the loss goes down efficiently and  it converges to a lower value  so again i did go through this quite  quickly and i strongly recommend  checking out the course notes to see  this in more detail and to experiment  with the code yourself and see what you  know what the errors look like and how  you can approach them  um but i've given you i hope i've given  you here a quick summary of  the most common bugs and maybe the most  common debris approaches to dealing with  them so good luck and remember to take  plenty of breaks if your code is giving  you a hard time


